Debith's direction (2026-09-12, settled 2026-09-13): during work, memories record what was learned, concretely and with the case. When the user asks for a consolidation — at any point, not only at a session's end — the agent reads back what the session wrote and states once, at the level the cases support, a pattern several of them share. Design: overview §4.11, section 00a Feature 7, section 01 §4 and §8.

Built (2026-09-13): `remember` takes `generalises` — two or more heads, which stay heads and count as read; the service refuses one case, a non-head, an instance also superseded by the same write, and a generalisation that does not cover its instances on every hard dimension (a dimension's `any` covers everything, so overreach is caught in review). `review(session)` lists a session's writes with what already generalises each. The MCP server serves the steps as the `consolidate` prompt, started by the user; it was deliberately not named "close session".

Still open (overview §10): whether a context spends budget on a generalisation's instances; what a later contradicting case should trigger.